# Phase 18 finite negative inner-message cursor rewind

Recorded: 2026-10-24 08:50 UTC
Branch: phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure
Code commit: 924466d6 fix(common): follow finite inner message cursor rewinds
Pinned Java reference: RocketMQ 5.5.1 at efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9

## Change

`MessageDecoder.countInnerMsgNum` follows in-range negative-size cursor
rewinds. The invoked Java case advances from position 0 to 8, rewinds to 5
with size -3, reads the overlapping size 255, and fails while setting the
out-of-range position; Java leaves the cursor at 9. Rust returns the typed
incomplete-record error at position 9. Rust tracks visited offsets after the
first negative size and returns a typed error at a repeated position to avoid
Java's infinite loop for cyclic input. Zero-size input is also bounded at its
original position.

